              "target": "mars_point",
              "position": [
                -0.15,
                1.05,
                0.95
              ]
            }
          ],
          "changeMeaning": "Mars shifts position and the retrograde path trail is displayed to show the backward loop.",
          "narration": "But roughly every 26 months, Mars slows its eastward drift, halts, and reverses direction. It moves westward for about two months, tracing a distinct loop, before reversing again to resume its normal eastward journey."
        },
        {
          "clipName": "clip_sky_puzzle",
