          "changeMeaning": "Geocentric orbital mechanics are enabled and displayed on the table.",
          "narration": "In the geocentric model, Earth sits motionless at the center of the universe. To explain the retrograde loop, ancient astronomers proposed that Mars rides on a small spinning circle called an epicycle, which itself rides on a larger circle called the deferent."
        },
        {
          "clipName": "clip_geo_loop_mechanism",
          "audioClip": "retro_geo_loop",
          "autoAdvance": false,
          "changes": [
            {
